// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.flow-analysis closure row; rule.fn.closure [Fn-Value-Read]; CHG-0299; conf.closure-passed-by-value-keeps-borrow
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `c` borrows `x` exclusively. Passing `c` by value copies it (it owns no
// resource), so `c` still holds that borrow, and `deriv(c, x, exclusive)`
// stays `T`: reading `x` is refuted. Both tools used to drop `c`'s facts
// when it was passed, and faulted at the read instead (CHG-0299).

import std;

fn call_val(fn() : void f)
{
    f();
}

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto c = [x]() { x = x + 1; };
    call_val(c);
    printf("%v\n", x);
}
